.TH CHTTP_BASE64_DECODE 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
chttp_base64_decode \- decode a base64 string (default allocator)
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/chttp.h>

void *chttp_base64_decode(const char *b64_input, size_t *out_len);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
This is a static inline wrapper around chttp_base64_decode_mp(). It
gives NULL for the memory management procedures, so the function uses
malloc and free.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
b64_input  The base64 string to decode. It ends with a NUL. It must
           not be NULL.
out_len    Optional. It gets the decoded byte length. Give NULL to
           ignore it.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
A new buffer with the decoded bytes, if the call succeeds.
NULL, if the allocation fails or if the input is malformed.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttp_base64_decode_mp (3),
.BR chttp_base64_encode (3)
